    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by **Isaac Paredes**, who commands the top efficiency score of 72.13. His matchup against Quantrill is ideal; the combination of a favorable 4.79 xERA opposing starter and a premier 3-hole placement in the order creates an elite ceiling for run production. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** (69.06) and **Seiya Suzuki** (68.99) are high-conviction plays. **Seiya Suzuki** specifically benefits from a 3% park factor boost and an impressive BvP history (26 PA), while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on the favorable xERA of Martinez. These three represent the core of our offensive output, projected to maximize our scoring across the RBI and HR categories despite varying levels of speed contribution.\n\nThe decision to bench **Austin Riley** (57.87) was the most difficult call on today's roster, as he sat just outside our active starting criteria. While his raw metrics remain respectable, the optimizer prioritized the higher efficiency of our active outfielders and the dynamic platoon advantages afforded to **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Corbin Carroll**. Even with **Corbin Carroll** facing the hurdle of a \"Slow SP\" designation (60% SB hold rate), his base projection remains high enough to warrant the start over the bench options. We are also monitoring the speed-focused profile of **Jose Caballero**; his 56.60 score is buoyed significantly by a massive 13% platoon edge against the opposing lefty, making him a critical weapon for our league-leading pursuit of SBs.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of our lower-score starters. **Dalton Rushing** (48.15) and **Cole Young** (47.78) are operating near the bottom of our threshold, and while both are active, they require close monitoring as game caps are thin. We are wary of the aggressive battery opposition facing **Zach McKinstry** (benched), and we have opted to keep **Henry Bolte** (40.55) and **Edwin Arroyo** (42.22) in reserve, as their floor-level projections do not provide the necessary margin over our primary starters. Should any late-breaking lineup changes occur\u2014particularly regarding **Travis Bazzana** or **Mickey Moniak**\u2014we are positioned to pivot to the bench, but for now, the data favors the current configuration to maintain our competitive edge in 5x5 Roto.",
